Patch summary:
Stop forcing ASTC emulation on hosts that support ASTC natively.

needEmulatedAstc() spot-checks a few ASTC formats before trusting the host, and
required VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_BIT and
VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR_BIT in *both* linearTilingFeatures
and optimalTilingFeatures. Vulkan does not require block-compressed formats to be
usable with VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR, and drivers do not expose them that way, so
the linear half of the test can never pass and every host falls through to the
emulated decompression path regardless of native support.

On Honeykrisp (Apple M1/M2) the host reports textureCompressionASTC_LDR = true
with optimalTilingFeatures = SAMPLED_IMAGE | SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR |
BLIT_SRC | TRANSFER_SRC | TRANSFER_DST for the ASTC LDR formats, and
linearTilingFeatures = 0. The GPU decompression path is used anyway, and it
mis-decodes some footprints: VK_FORMAT_ASTC_6x5_UNORM_BLOCK renders as vertical
stripes of block noise, so games shipping 6x5 textures (CarX Street) show corrupt
surfaces while geometry, lighting, and vector UI draw correctly.

Check optimal tiling only. Sampled images are always created with
VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL, so that is the property which reflects whether the host
can sample the format. Hosts without native ASTC still report
textureCompressionASTC_LDR = false and keep the emulation path, and this also
skips a full decompression pass per texture where the hardware can do the work.

diff --git a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder_global_state.cpp b/host/vulkan/vk_decoder_global_state.cpp
--- a/host/vulkan/vk_decoder_global_state.cpp
+++ b/host/vulkan/vk_decoder_global_state.cpp
@@ -10447,9 +10447,13 @@
             VkFormatProperties props;
             vk->vkGetPhysicalDeviceFormatProperties(physicalDevice, format, &props);
 
-            if ((props.linearTilingFeatures & requiredTilingFeatures) != requiredTilingFeatures ||
-                (props.optimalTilingFeatures & requiredTilingFeatures) != requiredTilingFeatures) {
-                // Linear tiling is not supported, emulate
+            // Only optimal tiling is relevant here. Sampled images are always created with
+            // VK_IMAGE_TILING_OPTIMAL, and Vulkan does not require block-compressed formats
+            // to be usable with VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR. Requiring linear support made this
+            // test fail on every driver, forcing emulation even with native ASTC.
+            if ((props.optimalTilingFeatures & requiredTilingFeatures) !=
+                requiredTilingFeatures) {
+                // The host cannot sample the format natively, emulate
                 return true;
             }
         }
